WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.860
- Paris is getting married,
so congratulations.

00:00:01.860 --> 00:00:02.991
- [Kelly] That's so exciting!

00:00:02.991 --> 00:00:03.824
- [Hilton] Thank you.

00:00:03.824 --> 00:00:04.657
- [Kelly] So, are you helping with that?

00:00:04.657 --> 00:00:06.420
- (crowd claps)

00:00:06.420 --> 00:00:08.610
- I am really- I'm just looking at myself.

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:10.440
Gosh, I need my roots done.

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.480
- [Kelly] You look amazing.

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:13.540
Oh my God. You should see
yourself, how I see you.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:15.499
You walked in and I was
like fabulous, okay.

00:00:15.499 --> 00:00:16.390
- Thank you.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.223
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:17.223 --> 00:00:18.590
- My hair gets really
frizzy in this weather.

00:00:18.590 --> 00:00:20.000
- [Kelly] Oh, mine does too, who cares?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:21.420
- Right. Who cares?

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:22.700
- [Kelly] Yeah, you look
great. Yeah. Do you-

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.070
But you're great at
like planning and stuff,

00:00:24.070 --> 00:00:24.903
So I figured you'd probably

00:00:24.903 --> 00:00:26.190
help with her wedding stuff, right?

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:30.070
- [Hilton] I am helping,
but I've hired Mindy Weiss

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:31.570
to hold my hand.

00:00:31.570 --> 00:00:32.403
- Ah.

00:00:32.403 --> 00:00:34.073
- Because I am A.D.D.

00:00:34.073 --> 00:00:34.906
- (crowd laughs)

00:00:34.906 --> 00:00:35.739
- [Kelly] Oh, I'm A.D.H.D.

00:00:35.739 --> 00:00:37.510
- E F G, and so is Paris.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:38.343
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:38.343 --> 00:00:41.070
- And I know I can get- I
could do it all on my own.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:41.903
- Yeah.

00:00:41.903 --> 00:00:44.720
- But then I would lose the guest list,

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.980
and it's got to be seated at some point.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.816
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:47.816 --> 00:00:48.649
- You do have to seat people.

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:50.830
- [Kelly] Yes, people
get weird about seating.

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.382
- You know what though?

00:00:52.382 --> 00:00:53.960
I believe that people like a home.

00:00:53.960 --> 00:00:56.820
They like to know they have a place to go.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:57.840
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.520
- Because if they don't, like
I know that my husband and I,

00:01:00.520 --> 00:01:04.270
when we go to a party, I'll
stop talking with this group,

00:01:04.270 --> 00:01:05.360
this group, this group.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:08.760
And then I'm standing there
with my plate of food.

00:01:08.760 --> 00:01:10.450
And then I walk up and all of a sudden,

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.800
there's one chair left
at this table, one there.

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:14.120
And he's like, Kathy, you're sitting there

00:01:14.120 --> 00:01:16.876
talking with everybody and
we're at different tables.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:17.709
So, sorry.

00:01:17.709 --> 00:01:18.917
- Oh. But that's kind of exciting.

00:01:18.917 --> 00:01:20.404
You talk to each other
all the time, you know?

00:01:20.404 --> 00:01:21.396
- (crowd laughs)

00:01:21.396 --> 00:01:22.680
- And you don't Want your husband,

00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:24.230
or your boyfriend or your girl, whatever,

00:01:24.230 --> 00:01:26.473
sitting next to somebody
that you don't like.

00:01:26.473 --> 00:01:27.306
- (crowd laughs)

00:01:27.306 --> 00:01:28.139
- Or it's kind of nice though,

00:01:28.139 --> 00:01:29.877
because then you get, well, there's that,

00:01:29.877 --> 00:01:30.710
- (crowd laughs)

00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.461
but then there, but then there's also,

00:01:32.461 --> 00:01:33.294
you get to like talk to people,

00:01:33.294 --> 00:01:34.670
you probably heard each
other stories, a ton.

00:01:34.670 --> 00:01:36.217
So you're like, I'm more
interested in this one.

00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:38.260
- You know what? I just
want to be with my friends.

00:01:38.260 --> 00:01:40.275
- I'd probably just take the
plate and hang with myself.

00:01:40.275 --> 00:01:41.203
- (crowd laughs)

00:01:41.203 --> 00:01:42.220
- I just want to eat my food, really.

00:01:42.220 --> 00:01:43.460
That's all I want to do.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:44.626
- I love it. But so-

00:01:44.626 --> 00:01:45.459
- I went to a corner.

00:01:45.459 --> 00:01:47.241
- She didn't actually,
When Paris was here,

00:01:47.241 --> 00:01:48.581
she is actually super cool,
like, congratulations.

00:01:48.581 --> 00:01:49.414
Like, What a kind individual.

00:01:49.414 --> 00:01:50.751
- She said say hi, and she sends her love.

00:01:50.751 --> 00:01:51.584
- (crowd clapping)

00:01:51.584 --> 00:01:52.910
- [Kelly] Like she's such a kind person.

00:01:52.910 --> 00:01:55.680
And I thought she doesn't come
across as like a bridezilla.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.382
She, she kind of-

00:01:57.382 --> 00:01:58.982
- She is easy breezy.

00:01:58.982 --> 00:02:00.199
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:02:00.199 --> 00:02:01.032
- It's him. I love him-

00:02:01.032 --> 00:02:02.031
- [Kelly] Oh, I love it.

00:02:02.031 --> 00:02:03.350
- But I'm gonna tell you people,

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:04.500
- [Kelly] It's the guy.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:07.730
- This guy is, I call him an octopus.

00:02:07.730 --> 00:02:11.170
He's got those mitts in everything.

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:12.360
- Oh, he likes to, Yeah.

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:15.960
- [Hilton] He, I call
Him Octopus Groomzilla.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:17.210
he's an O.G.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:19.380
- Oh my Gosh. You know what?
They're imperfect though.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:21.610
She's kind of breezy about
it. So one of them had to be.

00:02:21.610 --> 00:02:24.280
- She, I yelled at her
the other day and I said,

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.440
Paris, you know what?

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:28.870
This is ridiculous. I am
the mother of the bride.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.030
I am planning this wedding with you.

00:02:32.030 --> 00:02:33.850
I said, if you were to
walk down the street

00:02:33.850 --> 00:02:36.240
and ask 100 people-

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:39.196
He went ahead and started
calling about the band.

00:02:39.196 --> 00:02:40.029
- (crowd laughs)

00:02:40.029 --> 00:02:42.540
About a hotel, about all
the different arrangements.

00:02:42.540 --> 00:02:46.190
I said, I am the mother of the bride.

00:02:46.190 --> 00:02:48.520
I would be mad if my mom said that to me.

00:02:48.520 --> 00:02:51.130
She goes, "No, he just means well."

00:02:51.130 --> 00:02:51.963
I would be like,

00:02:51.963 --> 00:02:54.470
"Mom, don't insult me and talk
about my fiance like that."

00:02:54.470 --> 00:02:55.830
- [Kelly] I love that.

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:56.663
- Yeah.

00:02:56.663 --> 00:02:59.424
- [Kelly] Well she recognizes,
you're both dominant maybe?

00:02:59.424 --> 00:03:00.282
- (laughs)

00:03:00.282 --> 00:03:01.945
Maybe she's like, I'm going to lay low.

00:03:01.945 --> 00:03:03.172
- (laughs)

